# AGENTS.md: {{ project_name }}

Instructions for AI agents (and a quick map for people). This is an evidence project: search, screen,
extract, aggregate, synthesize. Keep code small and documented; extend what exists.

## Commands

- Install: `uv sync --locked`
- Validate project files, manifest, claims and extraction records: `uv run reprokit validate`
- Quick check on made-up sources: `uv run reprokit quick-check`
- Check online that included DOIs resolve: `uv run reprokit verify-sources`
- Aggregate extraction records (no AI calls): `uv run reprokit evidence-run [--only <ids>] [--exclude <ids>]`
- Test: `uv run pytest`

## Where things live

| Path | Purpose | Agents may |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `project.yaml` | Purpose, confidentiality, audiences, the `evidence:` block | Edit only with the owner's approval |
| `evidence/manifest.yaml` | The only list of sources, with screening and verification status | Add candidates; change status only as the protocol says |
| `evidence/extraction_schema.yaml`, `evidence/extractions/` | Declared fields and one record per included source (screening pipeline only) | Add and update records |
| `synthesis.md` | Narrative findings; every claim cites `[@id]` | Draft; claims only from included, verified sources |
| `protocol.md` | Search, screening and extraction decisions | Append to the decision log |
| `cache/` | Local copies of sources (git-ignored) | Read and write; never commit |
| `compute.yaml`, `agents.yaml` | Compute limits, AI-use rules and costs (screening pipeline only) | Read; never loosen without the owner's approval |
| `outputs/` | Rebuildable results | Regenerate |

## Hard rules

- Never commit source documents (PDF, EPUB, DOC, DOCX, RTF, ODT, DjVu, MOBI, AZW3, PS, XPS) or full text of
  any source. They go in `cache/`, which is git-ignored; text transcriptions go in `cache/text/`.
- New manifest entries are `candidate`; only the screening step in `protocol.md` sets `included` or `excluded`.
- In a public repository a `confidential` source is rejected, a `restricted` source gives a warning, and a
  project package may appear only as an open pointer (`open` or `restricted` access, no extraction record).
- Never commit credentials or `.env`.
- Every claim in `synthesis.md` cites its source as `[@id]`; cite only sources that are `included` and at
  least `source-verified`. Do not invent sources or identifiers.
- Extraction records hold short fields in your own words with page or section locators, never bulk quotation.
- Record the cost of every AI screening or extraction step in `compute.yaml`. Warn and wait for the owner's
  go-ahead before anything estimated over $1.
- Never send confidential or restricted sources to an external AI service.
- Mark every result with its verification state (proposed, source-verified, fixture-tested, run on acquired
  data, independently reproduced).

## Derivative rules

- **May reuse:** aggregated results and short summaries in your own words, with each source's citation.
- **Must exclude:** full text and copyrighted material, confidential-class content, unreleased results.
- **Must stop** and ask for the owner's review before anything is published, deployed or submitted.
- Confidentiality class of this project: **{{ confidentiality }}**.
